{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 3, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review. The review identified several instances where the draft application introduces specific geometric details not present in the inventor's source disclosure.\n\nSpecifically, the claims, detailed description, and figure briefs characterize the perimeter member as terminating in a \"bearing face that is an end face,\" which is a structural limitation not provided by the inventor. The inventor described only a \"rigid loop or skirt.\" This unsupported detail improperly narrows the invention as claimed.\n\nFurthermore, multiple figure briefs specify a \"rectangular\" shape for the device's base and perimeter member. The inventor's disclosure is shape-neutral, describing only a \"rigid base.\" While the briefs note that this shape is a \"convention,\" the review instructions are clear that introducing a specific, unsupported shape—even with a disclaimer—is a disclosure-fidelity error. The depiction must remain as generic as the source disclosure.\n\nOther minor unsupported geometric details were found, such as the specific layout of components on the base, the depiction of the perimeter member as two \"legs\" that are \"flush\" with the base, and the specific attachment point for the flexible pulling element.\n\nTwo critical findings will be reported to address the most significant issues: the unsupported limitation in the claims and the pervasive, unsupported \"rectangular\" shape asserted in the figure briefs. Correcting these will align the draft with the inventor's disclosure. The remaining sections and claims were found to be otherwise consistent with the provided sources."}
