{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 3, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review. The draft is largely compliant, with all claims and descriptive text tracing back to the inventor's disclosure. However, I identified two instances of unsupported geometric detail in the figure briefs for the sectional views. Specifically, the briefs for FIG. 2 and FIG. 4 dictate the exact relative angles and directions for hatching, which constitutes a substantive assertion about the material properties or drawing conventions that is not supported by the inventor's source documents. These details must be neutralized to ensure all aspects of the application are fully supported. Other than these two findings, the application is internally consistent and faithful to the provided sources."}
